      resume: 'Schleswig-Holstein lies in the far north between the North Sea and the Baltic, and three questions about it appear in the citizenship test. The coat of arms shows two blue lions on gold for Schleswig and a white nettle leaf on red for Holstein. The state flag is blue, white and red. The capital is Kiel, not Lübeck, Flensburg or Husum. The state parliament is elected for five years, and you can vote in municipal elections from 16. The correct district is Nordfriesland. The question on civic education has a twist: in Schleswig-Holstein the right answer is the state commissioner for civic education (Landesbeauftragte), not a state agency (Landeszentrale) as in the other states. The head of government is the Minister-President, and there is no foreign ministry. If you have studied other states’ questions, this is the answer to relearn.',
